Once upon a time in a quiet mountain village, there lived a boy named Arin who repaired clocks with his grandfather. Their tiny shop sat between a bakery and an old library, and every clock inside ticked with a different rhythm.

One rainy evening, a traveler entered the shop carrying a broken silver pocket watch.

“Can you fix this?” the traveler asked.

Arin opened the watch carefully. Inside, instead of gears, he found a tiny folded map.

That night, curiosity kept him awake. He unfolded the map under candlelight and discovered it pointed toward the forest beyond the village — a place everyone avoided because strange lights were said to appear there after dark.
